Enough. Let me implement the fixes.

Actually, for aim assist, simplest: in `tryFire`, after computing dir, if input.isTouch && settings.aimAssist, iterate bots alive, compute angle between dir and bot center direction, choose smallest with angle < 6° and dist < 90, and nudge dir 40% toward it. This helps. But it changes bullet direction; need camera.getWorldDirection each pellet. We can compute an `assistDir` per shot before loop:

```js
const aimAssist = this.game.input?.isTouch && this.profile.settings.aimAssist !== false;
let assistTarget = null;
if (aimAssist && this.game.bots) {
  const dir0 = this.camera.getWorldDirection(new THREE.Vector3());
  let best = 0.14; // ~8 degrees cosine
  for (const b of this.game.bots.bots) {
    if (!b.alive || b.team === 0 && ...) continue;
    const to = b.center().sub(this.camera.position);
    const d = to.length();
    if (d < 4 || d > 90) continue;
    to.normalize();
    const dot = to.dot(dir0);
    if (dot > best) { best = dot; assistTarget = to; }
  }
}
...
if (assistTarget) dir.lerp(assistTarget, 0.45).normalize();
```

But only when hip-firing? Aim assist on ADS maybe stronger. Fine. Need team check: in tdm avoid assisting teammates: `if (this.game.mode.id !== 'br' && b.team === 0) continue;` (player team 0). Actually player is team 0. In BR all bots hostile. Use same filtering as castShot: shooter is player; `shooter.team`? player doesn't have team. In TDM player should be team 0; bots team 0 are teammates. So skip `b.team === 0` when mode not br. Good.

This is a nice addition but risk: could cause weird snap through walls. The subsequent castShot ray tests walls so it's fine.

Let's implement it.

